      "text": "## 1. Complete Blood Count (CBC)"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#007",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nWHITE BLOOD CELL (WBC):\n  Normal: 4.5-11.0 × 10⁹/L\n  Differential:\n    Neutrophils 50-70%: bacterial infection (neutrophilia), chemotherapy (neutropenia)\n    Lymphocytes 20-40%: viral infections (lymphocytosis), CLL, lymphoma\n    Monocytes 2-8%: monocytosis in TB, fungal, monocytic leukemias\n    Eosinophils 1-4%: parasites, allergic, drug reactions, eosinophilic disorders\n    Basophils 0-1%: rare; IgE-mediated; CML (basophilia)\n  Left shift: immature neutrophils (bands/metamyelocytes) → suggests bacterial infection\n  Reactive lymphocytes: enlarged, irregular; EBV (infectious mono)"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#008",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RED BLOOD CELL (RBC) INDICES:\n  MCV (Mean Corpuscular Volume) — ANEMIA CLASSIFICATION KEY:\n    Microcytic (<80 fL): Iron deficiency (#1), thalassemia, anemia of chronic disease (usually normocytic)\n    Normocytic (80-100 fL): ACD, hemolytic, aplastic, early iron/B12 deficiency\n    Macrocytic (>100 fL): B12/folate deficiency (megaloblastic), hypothyroidism, liver disease, alcohol, reticulocytosis\n  MCHC (Mean Corpuscular Hemoglobin Concentration): elevated in hereditary spherocytosis\n  RDW (Red Cell Distribution Width): elevated = mixed population; iron deficiency early + B12 deficiency mix"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#009",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Reticulocyte count: assess bone marrow response\n    High reticulocyte %: adequate marrow response → hemolysis or acute blood loss\n    Low reticulocyte + low Hgb: bone marrow failure, B12/folate/iron deficiency, aplastic"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#010",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HEMOGLOBIN + HEMATOCRIT:\n  Anemia: Hgb <12 (women), <13 (men) g/dL\n  Polycythemia: Hgb >16.5 (men), >16 (women); primary (PV) vs secondary (EPO-driven)"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#011",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PLATELETS:\n  Normal: 150-400 × 10⁹/L\n  Thrombocytopenia (<150):\n    Immune (ITP): isolated; peripheral destruction; test for anti-platelet antibodies\n    HIT (Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia): 5-10 days after heparin; paradoxically THROMBOTIC\n      PF4-heparin antibody → activates platelets → thrombosis; stop ALL heparin; use argatroban\n    TTP (Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura): ADAMTS13 deficiency; microangiopathic hemolytic anemia\n      Pentad: fever, low plt, hemolytic anemia, renal failure, neuro changes → PLASMA EXCHANGE STAT\n    DIC: consumption; see below\n  Thrombocytosis: reactive (iron deficiency, infection, post-splenectomy) vs essential thrombocythemia (ET)\n```"
    },
