      "text": "## 2. Metabolic Panels (BMP/CMP)"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#014",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nBASIC METABOLIC PANEL (BMP):\n  Na+: 135-145 mEq/L\n    Hyponatremia: assess osmolality and volume status → SIADH vs hypothyroid vs adrenal vs redistribution\n    Hypernatremia: water deficit; central/nephrogenic DI; hyperaldosteronism\n  K+: 3.5-5.0 mEq/L\n    Hypokalemia: diarrhea, vomiting, diuretics, hyperaldosteronism, renal tubular acidosis\n    Hyperkalemia: renal failure, ACEi/ARBs/potassium-sparing diuretics, adrenal insufficiency, rhabdomyolysis\n  Cl-: 95-105 mEq/L; HCO3-: 22-29 mEq/L"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#015",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ANION GAP: AG = Na - (Cl + HCO3); normal 8-12 mEq/L\n  Elevated AG metabolic acidosis (MUDPILES):\n    Methanol, Uremia, DKA, Propylene glycol / Paraldehyde, Isoniazid / Iron, Lactic acidosis, Ethanol / Ethylene glycol, Salicylates\n  Non-anion gap (hyperchloremic) metabolic acidosis: diarrhea, RTA, early renal failure, carbonic anhydrase inhibitors"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md#016",
      "path": [
        "10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging, git-history:medicine:10-diagnostics-imaging]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "current_path": "medicine/10-DIAGNOSTICS-IMAGING.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:diagnostics-imaging",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[diagnostics, imaging]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "10 - Diagnostics and Imaging",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BUN/CREATININE + eGFR:\n  BUN: 7-25 mg/dL; creatinine: 0.6-1.2 mg/dL (M), 0.5-1.1 (F)\n  BUN:Cr ratio >20: pre-renal (dehydration, GI bleed with protein reabsorption)\n  eGFR: CKD-EPI formula (best for clinical use); normal >90 mL/min/1.73m²\n    CKD stages: G1 (eGFR ≥90), G2 (60-89), G3a (45-59), G3b (30-44), G4 (15-29), G5 (<15)\n  Creatinine limitations: muscle mass affects baseline; doesn't rise until ~50% renal function lost"
    },
